  "liner": {
   "body_md": "This recording captures Mountain Goats performing at WAVE in Wichita, Kansas, on July 17, 2022 [1]. Taped and transferred by the uploader, the soundboard audio documents a 108-minute set comprising twenty-one songs [1]. The performance includes tracks from various albums, such as “Aulon Raid” from Songs for Pierre Chuvin and “Color in Your Cheeks” from All Hail West Texas [1]. Notable moments include “Orange Ball of Love,” which is rare in the archive with only eleven recorded performances, and “Waylon Jennings Live!,” which is the only archived performance of that song [1]. The setlist also features “Getting Into Knives,” another song with a singular archived appearance [1]. The uploader notes that the room microphone capture was lost due to a faulty SD card, resulting in a dry sound that lacks crowd noise [1]. To compensate for this, mid/side imaging was applied to the audio, though the uploader acknowledges that the original crowd excitement cannot be recovered [1]. Despite the technical limitation, the recording is the only available capture of this specific show, which is the 345th in the archive’s collection for the band [1][2]. The set concludes with an encore featuring songs like “Let Me Bathe in Demonic Light” and “No Children” [1].",
